summary:
- topic: Budget Outlook and Public Engagement
  text: The Board Chair highlighted that the upcoming budget year will be difficult
    and encouraged broad public participation in the Public School Budget Forum on
    January 22nd, emphasizing its impact on all taxpayers.
- topic: SPHS Graduation Plans
  text: SPHS Principal Sarah Glenn presented graduation plans for 2026 (at Martin
    Field with a rain date) and 2027 (at Cross Insurance Arena due to athletic complex
    construction), noting the preference for venues with unlimited seating for families.
- topic: South Portland Middle School Field Remediation
  text: Director of Operations and Safety Mike Nalli updated the Board on the plan
    to remediate the SPMS field through aeration, overseeding, and fertilizing, asserting
    that the school department will not bear the cost and is withholding payment from
    contractors. Board members expressed concerns about the field's quality and the
    need for stronger action against contractors.
- topic: Support for Immigrant Families and Staff
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina reinforced the district's commitment
    to safety and belonging for all students, regardless of immigration status, and
    announced upcoming staff training with the University of Maine's Refugee and Human
    Rights Clinic. Public commenters and board members urged accelerated training
    and clearer public statements to address fears among vulnerable families and staff.
- topic: Superintendent Search Process
  text: The Board approved a contract with Zeal for the superintendent search, including
    national advertising through AASA and comprehensive background checks for finalists.
    Discussions highlighted the importance of a thorough search to find a long-term
    leader.
- topic: Policy Updates
  text: The Board approved the second reading of Policy BCA (School Board Member Ethics)
    and accepted the first reading of Policy BEDH (Public Participation at Board Meetings).
    The temperature control policy was referred back to the Buildings & Grounds Committee
    for further refinement.
- topic: School Calendar Postponement
  text: The approval of the School Calendar for the 2026-27 school year and an additional
    school day was postponed to the February meeting, pending negotiations with the
    service employees' union regarding the impact of the extra day.
- topic: Budget Freeze Impact and Phones in Schools
  text: Board members requested an update on the lived experience of the current spending
    freeze on principals and teachers. There was also a strong call to prioritize
    a discussion on the issue of phones in schools, with a suggestion to initiate
    this through the policy committee.
